# FINDINGS — seat 08, area 8 (THE CLOCK)

| id | area | finding | evidence file with the command that shows it again | status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 08-F1 | 8 | On a clock the tail is ~4x the median: 10 s clock, median 345 ms but p99 1335 ms and max 2426 ms, and 46 of 200 searches run past the engine's own soft limit (529 ms, up to 4.6x); none pass its hard limit (2645 ms). 1 s clock: median 40 ms, p99 153 ms, max 199 ms, 63 of 200 past soft. | job1/raw2/limits_table.txt, from `cd forge-combo29/swarm/08/job1 && python3 limits_vs_wall.py raw2`; raw searches job1/raw2/tc10000.jsonl | NEW |
| 08-F2 | 8 | `go movetime T` searches for T - Move Overhead, not T: 200 searches at movetime 50 gave median 40.5 ms (max 47.2), at movetime 500 median 490.5 ms (max 491.1), because search.cpp:2191-2193 sets hard = movetime - overhead with Move Overhead default 10. A cross-engine "movetime 50" match gives Forge 20 % less time. | job1/raw2/analysis_table.txt, from `python3 analyse_job1.py raw2` | NEW |
| 08-F3 | 8 | One of the 200 timing positions (index 3 of O) is answered from the built-in opening book in 0.02-0.36 ms (`info string book move e1g1`) with OwnBook at its default true, so a latency harness that leaves the book on mixes book answers into its table. | job1/raw/book_count.txt, from `python3 count_book.py ~/builds/release/forge OG200.fens /tmp/book.txt` | NEW |
| 08-F4 | 8 | Two identical 200-search runs at movetime 50 differ by 16.37 ms of 8000 ms (0.20 %), medians 40.5 vs 40.4 ms; so under ~1 % of total time on this 4-core box is noise and a speed claim needs more than one run per side. | job1/raw2/analysis_table.txt (baseline repeatability block), `python3 analyse_job1.py raw2` | NEW |
| 08-F5 | 8 | With 10 ms or less on the clock (`time <= Move Overhead`, default 10) the plan is reserve-empty and the search collapses to the play-or-search emergency branch: a legal TT move with 0 nodes (search.cpp:2302-2309), else max_depth 1 with a 2000-node cap (search.cpp:2310-2319). Measured: wtime 10/1/0 answer in 0.14-0.17 ms median, and the wtime 1 answer equals the `go depth 1` answer 8 of 8 while the first legal move only 1 of 8. A `winc 10` on a `wtime 10` clock does NOT lift it out of reserve-empty, because the reserve test runs before the increment is used. | job2/probe_no_clock.txt, from `cd forge-combo29/swarm/08/job2 && python3 probe_no_clock.py ~/builds/release/forge`; table job2/raw2/analysis_table.txt | NEW |
| 08-F6 | 8 | At `wtime 30 btime 30 winc 0` the plan is soft 1 ms / hard 1 ms and 108 of 200 searches exceed it (median 1.05, max 1.54 ms) — the only control of the ten where the engine's own hard limit is not respected. It still never exceeded the 30 ms clock. | job2/raw2/analysis_table.txt, `python3 analyse_job2.py raw2` | NEW |
| 08-F7 | 8 | At no control of `wtime 100/30/10/1/0` with `winc 0` or `winc 10` did any of 2,000 searches exceed the clock it was given, and 0 of 2,000 bestmoves were illegal. The inc-10 plan is larger than inc-0 at 100 ms (+6.8 ms median) and 30 ms (+5.8), and identical at 10/1/0 because reserve-empty ignores the increment. | job2/raw2/analysis_table.txt | NEW |
| 08-C1 | CONFIRMS seat 06 S-F4 | check_S06F4.md, raw check_S06F4_GR453.txt (again: `cd forge-combo29/swarm/08 && python3 check_s06f4.py ~/builds/release/forge /tmp/GR453.fens /tmp/out.txt`) | On 453 positions (all 353 G + 100 of my R_seed801) a left-right flip changes the static score of 444/453 = 98.0 % by hce and 450/453 = 99.3 % by total; median delta 20 cp hce (their figure exactly), 38 cp total; largest 738 cp on `5Q2/2k5/8/4KB2/7P/4R3/8/8` (equal material). Their 60 cp median and 838 cp max are higher than mine on a different position set — not a contradiction. Their S-F5 cancel case reproduced as my 3 unchanged totals. |
| 08-C2 | CONFIRMS seat 27 S-F2 | check_S27F2.md, raw check_S27F2_raw.txt + check_S27F2_threshold.txt (again: `cd forge-combo29/swarm/08 && python3 check_s27f2.py ~/builds/release/forge /tmp/o.txt`) | `go nodes 1..25` at startpos all answer a2a3 with 0 info lines, `go nodes 26` answers d2d4 with `info depth 1 ... nodes 26` — their boundary confirmed exactly; controls: `go nodes 700000` gives 17 info lines, and N=1 is identical in two fresh processes. BEYOND theirs: the boundary is position-dependent, not 26 — the smallest N printing an info line is 26 at startpos, 155 on a 51-move position, 394 on kiwipete, 38 in a rook endgame and 21 on a mate-in-1, so "N < 26 is the dead zone" is only true at startpos. |
